      "text": "The compass trembled and refused The pencil broke the margins bruised"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.0,
      "end": 83.0,
      "text": "And every line I thought was long I was just a wish somebody saw"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.0,
      "end": 90.0,
      "text": "The cartographer lied to me No safe blew where the reef should be"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.0,
      "end": 99.0,
      "text": "No sheltered mouth no gentle and no marked return No waiting friend the cart"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.0,
      "end": 106.0,
      "text": "The photographer lied but still I kept the ore against my will"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.0,
      "end": 115.0,
      "text": "If no one drew the stretch of foam then I will earn it by the bone"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.0,
      "end": 122.0,
      "text": "I passed the place the ships had crossed Well almost safe became a trade"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.0,
      "end": 130.0,
      "text": "I found the smoke I left behind Still practicing the shape it made"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.0,
      "end": 136.0,
      "text": "I thought a who could make me clean a crowded mercy In between but no drawn arrow tells the truth"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.0,
      "end": 141.0,
      "text": "Oh what you carry from the roof So I tore the corner from the chart"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.0,
      "end": 150.0,
      "text": "It tied around my heart and not for faith and not for proof Just to keep the weather out the sea is grammar paper lies"
    },
